  /* SURF PAGE */
  'surf.hero.title':'Surf Midigama','surf.hero.sub':'A peeling left across the road and a dozen more within a tuk-tuk ride. This is one of the best stretches of coast in Sri Lanka.',
  'surf.spot.eyebrow':'The break','surf.spot.title':'The wave out front.','surf.spot.body':'Directly across the road, a long, mechanical left-hander wraps over the reef, the kind of wave you can surf until your arms give out. It works best from mid to high tide and suits confident intermediates and up. For beginners and bigger days, the bay at Weligama is fifteen minutes west.',
  'surf.season.eyebrow':'When to come','surf.season.title':'Season & swell.',
  'surf.season.body':'The south coast turns on from November to April, with clean offshore mornings and chest-to-overhead sets. The shoulders of the season, November and April, are quieter and just as good. May to October the wind swings onshore and the crowd thins to almost nobody.',
  'surf.lessons.eyebrow':'Coaching & packages','surf.lessons.title':'Surf with us.',
  'surf.faq.eyebrow':'Good to know','surf.faq.title':'Surf questions, answered.',
  'surf.q1':'What level do I need to surf the spot out front?','surf.a1':'The left out front is a reef break and rewards confident intermediates and above, you should be comfortable paddling out, reading a set, and riding along the face. Newer surfers are in great hands too: we run beginner sessions in the sandy-bottomed bay nearby.',
  'surf.q2':'When is the best time to come?','surf.a2':'December to March is the heart of the season, consistent swell, light morning winds, warm water. November and April are quieter shoulders with plenty of good days.',
  'surf.q3':'Do you rent boards?','surf.a3':'Yes. We keep a quiver of shortboards, fish, and a few mid-lengths and longboards for guests. If you\'d rather travel light, just tell us your height, weight and level and we\'ll have the right board waiting.',
  'surf.q4':'Is the water warm?','surf.a4':'Year-round. The water sits around 27–29°C, so boardshorts or a bikini are all you need, no wetsuit, ever.',

  /* YOGA PAGE */
  'yoga.hero.title':'Yoga at Naia','yoga.hero.sub':'A rooftop shala open to the sky and the sound of the sea. Practice at sunrise, again at sunset, or simply when you feel like it.',
  'yoga.prog.eyebrow':'The practice','yoga.prog.title':'Move, breathe, soften.',
  'yoga.prog.body':'We teach a warm, unhurried practice on the open rooftop shala. Mornings are dynamic vinyasa to wake the body before the surf; evenings drop into slow yin and long, quiet breathwork as the light goes. All levels are welcome, come as you are, leave a little lighter.',
  'yoga.retreat.eyebrow':'Retreats','yoga.retreat.title':'Stay a little longer.',
  'yoga.teacher.eyebrow':'Your teacher','yoga.teacher.title':'Led with care.',
  'yoga.teacher.name':'Maya','yoga.teacher.role':'Lead teacher · 500h RYT',
  'yoga.teacher.bio':'Maya has taught between the mountains of Rishikesh and the coasts of Sri Lanka for over a decade. Her classes are grounded, intuitive and gently challenging, rooted in alignment, carried by breath. She believes a strong practice should still feel like coming home.',
  'yoga.sched.eyebrow':'A typical week','yoga.sched.title':'Weekly schedule.',
